The monitoring folder is just like a folder on your Windows desktop. Inside it, you'll create multiple Python files.

Your project will eventually look like this:

ACTDRS/
│
├── app.py
├── requirements.txt
│
├── monitoring/
│      ├── cpu_monitor.py
│      ├── ram_monitor.py
│      ├── disk_monitor.py
│      └── process_monitor.py
│
├── logs/
├── config/
├── ai/
├── response/
└── dashboard/
How to create a Python file inside a folder?

There are 3 methods. I'll teach you all of them.

Method 1 (Recommended): Using VS Code ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐

This is how professional developers usually do it.

Step 1

Open your ACTDRS folder in VS Code.

From the Ubuntu terminal:

code .

The . means "open the current folder".

Step 2

On the left side, you'll see:

ACTDRS
│
├── monitoring
├── ai
├── logs
...
Step 3

Right-click on the monitoring folder.

Choose:

New File
Step 4

Type:

cpu_monitor.py

Press Enter.

Done! 🎉

Now create:

ram_monitor.py

Then:

disk_monitor.py

Then:

process_monitor.py
Method 2: Using the Terminal ⭐⭐⭐⭐

Suppose you're already inside the ACTDRS folder.

Create a file like this:

touch monitoring/cpu_monitor.py

This creates:

monitoring/
    cpu_monitor.py

Similarly:

touch monitoring/ram_monitor.py
touch monitoring/disk_monitor.py
touch monitoring/process_monitor.py
Method 3: Using Nano (Terminal Text Editor) ⭐⭐⭐

Create and edit the file in one step:

nano monitoring/cpu_monitor.py

A text editor opens.

Paste your Python code.

To save:

Press Ctrl + O
Press Enter

To exit:

Press Ctrl + X
Which method should you use?

Since this is your first software project, I recommend:

✅ VS Code

Because later you'll have:

50+ Python files
Hundreds of lines of code
AI models
HTML
CSS
JavaScript

VS Code makes all of that much easier to manage.

